We have, $\frac{\cos A}{a}=\frac{\cos B}{b}=\frac{\cos C}{c}\begin{aligned}
\Rightarrow & & \frac{\cos A}{k \sin A} & =\frac{\cos B}{k \sin B}=\frac{\cos C}{k \sin C} \\
\Rightarrow & & \cot A & =\cot B=\cot C \\
\Rightarrow & & A & =B=C=60^{{}^{\circ}}
\end{aligned}\therefore \triangle A B C$ is an equilateral triangle.
$\begin{aligned}
\therefore \text{ Area$ of $triangle } & =\frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} a^2 \\
& =\frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \times 2^2=\sqrt{3} \mathrm{sq} \text{ units }
\end{aligned}$
